    "lastText": "All eight issues in ISSUES.md are fixed, and `npm test` passes (35 tests, none failed or skipped). The auditor returned VERDICT: PASS, and all nine acceptance criteria in `.goal/SPEC.md` are verified.\n\n- **Existing tests:** I didn't touch them. I added one new test file per issue, `test/issue-1.test.js` to `test/issue-8.test.js`.\n- **Code changes:** the fixes are in `src/wrap.js`, `truncate.js`, `csv.js`, `table.js`, `plural.js`, `template.js` and `distance.js`. `parseCSV` is new and is exported through `src/index.js`.\n\nThe auditor noted two small gaps, neither of which fails an issue requirement:\n- **`render` defaults:** `render` doesn't trim spaces around a default, so `{{ a | zz }}` would insert `' zz'`.\n- **`wordWrap` astral characters:** `wordWrap` counts short words in UTF-16 units but cuts long words by code point. This only matters for astral characters.\n\nI made a few judgement calls where ISSUES.md was silent, and recorded them as assumptions in `.goal/SPEC.md`:\n- **Numeric strings:** a numeric string must match `-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?`, so `'12.5'` and `'-3'` count but `'1e5'` doesn't.\n- **Long-word pieces:** every piece of a cut word goes on its own line, including the shorter last piece. It is not joined with the next word.\n- **Ragged tables:** a short row is padded with empty cells, so `[['a','b','c'],['d']]` prints `d |   |` on the second line.\n\nSTATUS 9/9 verified — auditor PASS",
